      "writtenOn": "2019-09-09T23:01:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m not convinced the compiler won\u0027t ever do byte copy here if p256_int has attribute((packed))?\n\nUnless it emits run-time code to check that k_out is at word address and optimizes?\nOr it just emits memcpy, which then does the word copy optimization? Fragile..\n\nsomeone should refactor and get rid of attribute((packed)) for p256_int..",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 147,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 147,
        "endChar": 13
      },
      "revId": "bc508d407dab9c19d2747a1204a5f32884e29b2d",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "67dc770a_96c66b42",
        "filename": "chip/g/dcrypto/hmac_drbg.c",
        "patchSetId": 19
      },
      "lineNbr": 147,
      "author": {
        "id": 1256783
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-09-10T01:36:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I believe it emits memcpy\n\np256_int is used in parts of the TPM stack where it actually is unaligned, so we can\u0027t just remove packed (b/132132791); we could have a separate non-packed struct, and a function to safely copy between them, but I\u0027m not convinced that making the entire codebase compatible with writes to DMEM is the right way to go - eg we might want to use this function to write into an unaligned p256_int used in the TPM stack.\n\nIMHO the constraints around DMEM should be handled as close as possible to where the write happens, and the rest of the codebase should not need to know about this: \nhttps://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/1595928",
      "parentUuid": "1d52d5ef_a4fc2242",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 147,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 147,
        "endChar": 13
      },
      "revId": "bc508d407dab9c19d2747a1204a5f32884e29b2d",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f17db4a8_18cc136e",
        "filename": "chip/g/dcrypto/hmac_drbg.c",
        "patchSetId": 19
      },
      "lineNbr": 147,
      "author": {
        "id": 1308870
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-09-10T16:58:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "yeah, ideally this function should not interact with DMEM directly. all the writes to DMEM should happen via CP1W or CP8W from within the dcrypto_p256 module.",
      "parentUuid": "67dc770a_96c66b42",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 147,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 147,
